From e073a53f06095ca64a7aa60ffe2e1731a868c9ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:32:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] kanban: a tui row defers to its waking local sibling only
 until the wake delivers (no lost notice when the wake never lands)

Review of PR #1465 at 67d5fb1cfc: tui_cover silenced covered kinds because a waking local row existed, so in
notice-first order the tui row was acked past an event the wake still owed; a wake dropped after
MAX_SEND_FAILURES (or never claimed: no LOCAL adapter) lost the event. Now the tui consumers silence only events
at or below the local row's acknowledged cursor, and leave the tui row unclaimed (tui_defer) while the wake owes a
covered event younger than DEFER_MAX_S (600 s). The wake then carries the notice line and settles the tui row; a
dropped local row or an expired window hands the notice back to the tui row. Guards: both reviewer probes plus the
sweeper past the window. [daveey]
